        "translation": "How are you?",
        "audioOverride": "Shlonak?",
        "isFlashcardOption": true,
        "exampleTranslation": "Good morning, Mohammed, **how are you** today?"
      },
      {
        "id": 1769133772942,
        "text": "How do you say 'How are you?' to a woman in Emirati Arabic?\"",
        "sender": "user"
      },
      {
        "id": 1769133777762,
        "text": "This is a standard, informal greeting used specifically when addressing a woman in Emirati Arabic. The 'ج' (jīm) at the end replaces the standard Arabic 'ك' (kāf) for the feminine 'you', pronounced as a 'ch' sound.",
        "phrase": "شحالج؟",
        "sender": "ai",
        "example": "يا سلمى، **شحالج؟** عساج بخير اليوم؟",
        "translation": "How are you?",
        "audioOverride": "Sh-haal-ich?",
        "isFlashcardOption": true,
        "exampleTranslation": "Salma, **how are you?** Hope you are well today?"
      },
      {
        "id": 1769134645530,
        "text": "How are you? (feminine)\".",
        "sender": "user"
      },
      {
        "id": 1769134656272,
        "text": "This phrase is used to directly inquire about the well-being of a female in Emirati Arabic.",
        "phrase": "كيف حالچ؟",
        "sender": "ai",
        "example": "فاطمة، لم أراچ منذ فترة، **كيف حالچ؟** أتمنى أن كل شيء يسير على ما يرام.",
        "translation": "How are you? (feminine)",
        "audioOverride": "كيف حالچ؟",
        "isFlashcardOption": true,
        "exampleTranslation": "Fatima, I haven't seen you in a while, **how are you?** I hope everything is going well."
      }
    ],
